.TH "module:install" 1 "September 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
module:install \- Install, activate, and configure framework or application modules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php module:install
\fImodulename\fR
[\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIappName\fR]
[\fB\-\-project\fR=\fIprojectId\fR]
[\fB\-\-all\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmodule:install\fR activates and provisions modules across the SPP framework. Supports system modules in \fBspp/modules\fR as well as application-level extensions inside \fBsrc/{App}/modules\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fImodulename\fR
Name or directory slug of the module to install.
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIappName\fR
Target application context (e.g. SPPDocs).
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR=\fIprojectId\fR
Target project identifier for app-level modules (default: spp).
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Batch-install all active or discovered modules.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.IP \(bu 3
Updates module status configurations in \fBspp/etc/modules.yml\fR.
.IP \(bu 3
Executes database migrations and module lifecycle hooks (\fBmodinit.php\fR).
.IP \(bu 3
Invalidates and regenerates autoloader cache.
